#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0059.1-A expect=violation domain=PC
#note "R-5.25 split of SEND59.1 (top-level-or board wave 2, group J), the --ELTM split sibling: row 1's PCELTM is not a valid ISO 8601 duration (the negative-interval extension is accepted, so row 2 of the negative control carries -P1D) -> fires, named against this one variable instead of the three-name disjunction. The other rows are conformant."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 PCSEQ=1
dataset PC class=FINDINGS label="Pharmacokinetics Concentrations"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col PCSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col PCTESTCD type=Char label="Test Short Name"
col PCELTM type=Char label="Planned Elapsed Time"
---
S1 | PC | 001 | 1 | DRUGX | not-a-dur
S1 | PC | 001 | 2 | DRUGX | P1D
S1 | PC | 001 | 3 | DRUGX | -P1D
